2026-02-11 01:22:55,443 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document Factors That Affect a Put’s Price

The value of a put option generally decreases as it approaches expiration because of the impact of time decay. Time decay accelerates as an option’s expiration date gets closer, since there’s less time to profit from the trade.

When an option loses its time value, the intrinsic value is what's left. An option’s intrinsic value is equivalent to the difference between the strike price and the underlying stock price. An option is in the money (ITM) if it has intrinsic value. is relevant
